      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The quality of life was assessed in 36 patients with painful dysfunction of the temporomandibular joint (TMJ) and 73 patients with TMJ dysfunctions suffering from rheumatoid arthritis. A more significant negative time course of the parameters was observed in patients with rheumatoid arthritis and more positive shifts in patients with isolated TMJ dysfunction without rheumatoid arthritis."},
